This repository also holds third-party material used only by its tests. None of it is part of the published
@typesol/cli package.

- test/programs/: program binaries dumped from Solana clusters. The ones kept in the repository are Apache-2.0:
  SPL Account Compression and SPL Noop (solana-labs/solana-program-library), Program Metadata
  (solana-program/program-metadata), coral-xyz/multisig, Raydium CP-Swap, Raydium CLMM and Raydium AMM v4 (raydium-io), Jito's tip
  payment, tip distribution and priority fee distribution programs (jito-foundation/jito-programs), marginfi v2
  (mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2) and Solend's token-lending (solendprotocol/solana-program-library). The licence text is test/programs/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt; each binary's source, program id
  and sha256 are in test/programs/SOURCES.md.
  marginfi v2's Drift v2 test build (drift-labs/protocol-v2) is Apache-2.0 too and kept.
  The Metaplex programs, under the Metaplex(TM) NFT Open Source License 1.0, Kamino's lending and farms programs and
  JupLend's lending, liquidity and rewards programs, under the Business Source License 1.1, and Drift's Merkle
  distributor, under the GNU GPL 3.0, are not kept here: scripts/fetch-programs.sh downloads them.
- showcase/test/fixtures/marginfi/: Marginfi v2's on-chain IDL and three of its mainnet accounts (mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2,
  Apache-2.0), and I80F48 vectors written with the fixed crate (MIT or Apache-2.0).
- showcase/test/fixtures/kamino/: the IDLs of Kamino's lending (1.25.0) and farms programs, the interface descriptions
  as mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2 keeps them in idls-complete/ (Apache-2.0); the programs are not here (see above).
- showcase/test/fixtures/drift/, showcase/test/fixtures/juplend/: the IDLs of Drift v2 and of JupLend's lending,
  liquidity and rewards rate model programs, as mrgnlabs/marginfi-v2 keeps them in idls-complete/ (Apache-2.0).
- showcase/test/fixtures/clmm/: Raydium CLMM's on-chain IDL and the accounts of one mainnet pool (raydium-io/raydium-clmm,
  Apache-2.0).

Examples under examples/ that port these programs (raydium-cp-swap, raydium-clmm, raydium-amm, jito-mev, marginfi, multisig.ts)
follow their originals' source, which is Apache-2.0; see each file's header.
